.TH GEEKBENCH7-LINUX 1 "October 2026" "geekbench7-linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
geekbench7-linux \- unofficial packaging for official Geekbench 7 on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B geekbench7-linux
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B geekbench7-linux
downloads and launches the official, unmodified Geekbench 7 Linux build from
Primate Labs' CDN. It never redistributes or patches Geekbench.
.PP
Geekbench is made by Primate Labs (founder John Poole). This project is not
affiliated with Primate Labs. Please buy a license at
https://www.primatelabs.com/store/v7/ if you find Geekbench useful.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Download and extract Geekbench 7 (requires
.B --accept-eula
on first run).
.TP
.B run
Run the official
.B geekbench7
binary (default for the
.B geekbench7
alias).
.TP
.B update
Refresh the pinned Geekbench version from the CDN.
.TP
.B doctor
Report install paths, arch and status.
.TP
.B about
Credits, thanks and disclaimer.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove per-user Geekbench state (keeps the system package).
.TP
.B desktop install|remove
Install or remove a per-user menu entry.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://www.geekbench.com/
.br
https://github.com/ventura8/geekbench7-linux
